    {
      "text": "You can create user-related widgets in the dashboard and reports or when analyzing charts in Web, Mobile, Firewall, or DNS Insights. For example, you can create a report to view and export a list of users who browse the web the most."
    },
    {
      "text": "Excluding locations also applies to the Executive Report and all standard, user-related reports in Interactive Reports."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Excluding Locations in Widgets",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "By default, user-related widgets include locations and users. You can exclude locations by creating new or editing existing widgets and using the Exclude Location filter. This filter applies to all user-related widgets except for widgets in the default Security dashboard.",
      "strong": [
        [
          146,
          162
        ],
        [
          253,
          261
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "For example, if you edit the user-related widget Top Users in the Web Overview dashboard, choose the filter User and enable the Exclude Location toggle.",
      "strong": [
        [
          49,
          58
        ],
        [
          108,
          112
        ],
        [
          128,
          144
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "See image."
    },
    {
      "text": "When adding a new widget in a dashboard or report:"
    },
    {
      "item": "Select Web, Mobile, Firewall, or DNS in the New Widget window.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          10
        ],
        [
          12,
          18
        ],
        [
          20,
          28
        ],
        [
          33,
          36
        ],
        [
          44,
          54
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "From the Data Type drop-down menu, choose User.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          9,
          18
        ],
        [
          42,
          46
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Expand Add Filter and choose User.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 3,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          17
        ],
        [
          29,
          33
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Enable the Exclude Location toggle.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 4,
      "strong": [
        [
          11,
          27
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Click OK to save.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 5,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          8
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "See image."
